The selector is fine, but this often runs before the button exists. Run setup after DOM parsing and prevent a missing element from throwing.

```js
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
  const button = document.querySelector('#save');
  if (!button) return;
  button.addEventListener('click', () => console.log('saved'));
});
```

Clamp the value before updating the label.

```js
let n = 0;
minus.addEventListener('click', () => {
  n = Math.max(0, n - 1);
  count.textContent = String(n);
});
```

Check the response before parsing and handle non-2xx responses.

```js
async function load() {
  const response = await fetch('/api/items');
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Request failed: ${response.status}`);
  const text = await response.text();
  const items = text ? JSON.parse(text) : [];
  render(items);
}
```

Now an empty body becomes an empty list instead of being dereferenced.

A fixed percentage plus gaps can exceed the row. Let flex calculate three equal tracks and allow wrapping.

```css
.cards {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1rem;
}
.card {
  flex: 1 1 calc((100% - 2rem) / 3);
  min-width: 14rem;
}
```

Do not put untrusted input in `innerHTML`. Use a text node assignment.

```js
const name = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('name') ?? '';
document.querySelector('#greeting').textContent = name;
```

This renders markup as text and avoids HTML injection.

The rerender is registering another listener on the same node. Replace the handler, or initialize once with an `AbortController`.

```js
let inputController;
function mountInput(input) {
  inputController?.abort();
  inputController = new AbortController();
  input.addEventListener('input', update, { signal: inputController.signal });
}
```

Move clipping to an inner content wrapper. The card itself must allow overflow for the positioned tooltip.

```css
.card { border-radius: 12px; overflow: visible; }
.card-content { border-radius: inherit; overflow: hidden; }
.tooltip { position: absolute; z-index: 10; }
```

`sort()` mutates the original array, and your renderer may be comparing the same reference. Copy before sorting and render the new value.

```js
const sorted = [...items].sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
setItems(sorted);
```

Hide the links by default on narrow screens and reveal them with a class; keep the desktop layout in the media query.

```css
.nav-links { display: none; }
.nav-links.is-open { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
@media (min-width: 700px) {
  .nav-links { display: flex; flex-direction: row; }
  .menu-button { display: none; }
}
```

A date-only string is parsed as UTC, which can shift backward in local time. Parse its components as a local date.

```js
function displayDate(value) {
  const [year, month, day] = value.split('-').map(Number);
  return new Date(year, month - 1, day).toLocaleDateString();
}
```

`getItem` returns null on the first visit. Supply a default before parsing.

```js
const raw = localStorage.getItem('prefs');
const prefs = raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : { theme: 'light' };
```

For corrupt stored data, wrap the parse in `try/catch` and reset the default.

The line height is larger than the box. Use flex alignment, which also handles multiline changes cleanly.

```css
.button {
  min-height: 32px;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  padding-inline: 12px;
}
```

Use one guarded listener and close only when the modal is open.

```js
document.addEventListener('keydown', event => {
  if (event.key !== 'Escape') return;
  const modal = document.querySelector('.modal.is-open');
  modal?.classList.remove('is-open');
});
```

Custom properties inherit only through ancestors. Put the variable on `:root` for global use, then override it in a theme scope.

```css
:root { --brand: #2563eb; }
.theme-dark { --brand: #93c5fd; }
```

Ensure the element using the color is inside `.theme-dark` when you want the override.

A custom setter can bypass the browser's editing constraint. Enforce the limit at the input boundary and when assigning programmatically.

```js
function setMessage(value) {
  textarea.value = value.slice(0, 20);
}
textarea.addEventListener('input', () => {
  if (textarea.value.length > 20) textarea.value = textarea.value.slice(0, 20);
});
```

Keep the reset for mouse styling but add a clear keyboard-only focus ring.

```css
button:focus { outline: none; }
button:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid #f59e0b;
  outline-offset: 3px;
}
```

The ring appears when focus is keyboard-relevant without changing the button's layout.
